            "source_kind": "block_threads",
            "source_step": 1,
            "effect": "ignored:block_threads",
            "rationale": {
              "text": "Try the maximum 1024 threads/block. For N=4096, each thread handles exactly 4 elements. 1024 threads = 32 warps per block saturates the SM's warp scheduler; the per-row reduction is fully contained within one block, minimizing inter-block sync and maximizing L1/shared-memory reuse of W and B. This is the classic high-throughput layernorm configuration.",
              "lang": "en"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
